tg-sendmail (0.4.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Rewritten in Go for better performance and no runtime dependencies
  * Drop-in replacement for Python implementation
  * Configuration moved from INI to YAML
  * Accept the full set of sendmail options, including attached values
    (-froot@host) and options after recipients; unknown options are ignored
    instead of rejecting the message
  * Accept messages that do not start with headers
  * Report Telegram API failures instead of exiting successfully
  * Measure the message length in characters, so that non-ASCII messages are
    not split into an attachment too early or cut mid-character
  * Keep headers in the order they were submitted
  * Keep the bot token out of the world-readable log
  * Honour the configured log level
  * Time out API calls instead of hanging a cron job
  * Package is now architecture-dependent and built for amd64, arm64 and armhf
  * Log a line for every delivered message, so that an idle log can be told
    apart from a broken installation
  * Strip stray quotes and whitespace from the configured credentials
  * Explain the getUpdates conflict caused by a registered webhook
  * Migrate credentials from the pre-0.4.0 INI file on upgrade
  * Rotate /var/log/tg-sendmail.log, keeping it writable by every sender

 -- Oleg Smedyuk <oleg.smedyuk@gmail.com>  Sun, 16 Aug 2026 20:34:00 +0000

